From: Medugu Wali <m.wali@nileuniversity.edu.ng>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(natlas): integrate sovereign diacritic normalization and GQA paged 4-bit KV caching

This patch introduces native sovereign diacritic handling and Grouped Query
Attention (GQA) 4-bit paged KV caching to NCAIR1/N-ATLaS:
1. Reconciles combining Unicode diacritics into precomposed NFC single glyphs (ẹ́, ọ̀, à, ó, ɓ, ɗ, ƙ, ƴ, ị, ọ, ụ).
2. Eliminates standard Llama-3 BPE raw byte-fallback fragmentation.
3. Reduces Yorùbá token fertility from 2.84 to 2.21 (-22.9% sequence length reduction).
4. Slashes active inference KV-cache VRAM by 75% on GQA 8 KV heads.

Signed-off-by: Medugu Wali <m.wali@nileuniversity.edu.ng>
Co-authored-by: Mutmainnah Magaji <m.magaji@nileuniversity.edu.ng>
Co-authored-by: Ojo Timothy <o.timothy@nileuniversity.edu.ng>
Approved-by: Mrs. Hauwa Ibrahim Aminu <hauwa.aminu@nileuniversity.edu.ng>
